CONTRACT EMPLOYMENT AGREEMENT
THIS AGREEMENT, made and entered into this
____
day of August, 2019, by and between
the City of Cheyenne, Wyoming, a municipal corporation organized under the laws of the State of
Wyoming, acting by and through its political subdivision, the Cheyenne Police Department,
hereinafter referred to as the “Department,” and Jessica A. Fritz, hereinafter referred to as “Fritz.”
WITNESSETH:
WHEREAS, the Department is a law enforcement agency serving the City of Cheyenne, and
is a department thereof: and
WHEREAS, the Department has received a grant of funds from the Wyoming Division of
Victim Services for the purpose of providing crime victim assistance services; and
WHEREAS, in order to provide crime victim assistanëe services, the Department desires to
retain the services of a “Victim Assistance Advocate;” and
WHEREAS, because funding a Victim Assistance Advocate position is dependent on the
receipt of a grant, the Department wishes to create a contract employee rather than permanent
employee position; and
WHEREAS, Fritz has training and experience in the field of assisting crime victims; and
WHEREAS, Fritz desires to provide services to the Department under the terms and
conditions hereinafter contained.
NOW, THEREFORE, in consideration of the promises and mutual covenants herein, the
parties agree as follows:
1.
The term of this Agreement shall commence July 1st, 2019, and terminate June 30th,
2020, unless sooner terminated pursuant to Section 9 below or if grant funding is no longer available.
2.
Fritz will be considered a contract employee of the Department. She will act as
Victim Assistance Advocate and assist the Department.
3.
Fritz shall at all times coordinate her activities hereunder with the Department and
shall work under the direction of the Department.
4.
The Department agrees to pay Fritz the sum of Two Thousand Six Hundred Dollars
and Zero Cents ($2,600.00) per month. The total amount over the term of this agreement will not, in
any event, exceed the sum of Thirty-One Thousand Two Hundred Dollars and Zero Cents
($31,200.00).
5.
The Department shall provide Fritz the benefits provided to full-time employees of
the City of Cheyenne. The City of Cheyenne will withhold appropriate federal income and social
security taxes and remit them to the federal government.
6.
In addition to the compensation set forth above, the Department agrees to pay Fritz for
hours worked in excess of forty hours in a work week at time and one-half rate.
7.
In the event that the governing body authorizes a bonus to be paid to city employees.
Fritz would be eligible to receive a bonus similar to other city employees. Such bonus payment shall
first be made out of grant funds, if available, then out of Department funds, if grant funds are not
available.
8.
Fritz is subject to the City of Cheyenne Personnel Rules and Regulations, all federal
