and state laws, city ordinances and actions of the city’s governing body pertaining generally to city
employees, except that Fritz shall not be entitled to the procedural protections set forth in the
following sections of the City’s personnel rules: Chapter X, Section 3.C., last sentence; Chapter X,
Section 3.D.2; Chapter X, Section 3.D.3; Chapter XI; and Chapter XII, Section 23. and 2.C.
Because this contract is for one year and because the funding for the position is dependent on grant
funding, Fritz is not a permanent employee of the City of Cheyenne. It is mutually understood and
agreed that Fritz is employed on an “at will” basis and that her employment maybe terminated by the
Department, with or without cause.
9.
This Agreement may be terminated by the Department, with or without cause.
10.
Fritz agrees to comply with all applicable federal, state and local laws, rules and
regulations in the performance of this Agreement.
11.
if any provision, section, subsection, sentence, clause or phrase of this Agreement is
invalidated by any court of competent jurisdiction, the Agreement will automatically terminate.
12.
All parties acknowledge full opportunity for consultation with legal counsel regarding
